<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Loughrea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Loughrea is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-galway">County Galway</a> in the west of Ireland, on the shore of the lake from which it takes its name. Richard Mór de Burgh founded it around 1236 with a castle, and a Carmelite friary followed. It became the chief seat of the Clanricarde <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-burgh">Burkes</a>, the Upper Mac William lords of south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galway">Galway</a>, and remains of its medieval defences survive.</p></div>
